    "text": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.risk",
    "text": "INSTRUCTIONS PERTAINING TO RISK OF FIRE, ELECTRIC SHOCK, OR INJURY TO PERSONS",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.warn.l",
    "text": "WARNING:",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.warn.b",
    "text": "Always follow these basic precautions when using this product.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l1",
    "text": "Read all the instructions before using the product.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l2",
    "text": "To Reduce the Risk of Injury, close supervision is necessary when the product is used near children.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l3",
    "text": "Do not put fingers or hands into the product.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l4",
    "text": "Do not expose power bank to rain or snow.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l5",
    "text": "Do not expose power bank to heat or fire. Do not store in direct sunlight or in a vehicle.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l6",
    "text": "Use of a power supply or charger not recommended or sold by power bank manufacturer may result in a risk of fire or injury to persons.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l7",
    "text": "Do not use the power bank in excess of its output rating. Overload outputs above rating may result in a risk of fire or injury to persons.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l8",
    "text": "Do not use the power bank that is damaged or modified. Damaged or modified batteries may exhibit unpredictable behavior resulting in fire, explosion or risk of injury.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l9",
    "text": "Do not disassemble the power bank. Take it to a qualified service person when service or repair is required. Incorrect reassembly may result in a risk of fire or injury to persons.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l10",
    "text": "Do not expose a power bank to fire or excessive temperature. Exposure to fire or temperature above 60°C may cause explosion.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l11",
    "text": "Have servicing performed by a qualified service or repair person using only identical replacement parts. This will ensure that the safety of the product is maintained.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.l12",
    "text": "Switch off the power bank when not in use.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.save",
    "text": "SAVE THESE INSTRUCTIONS",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.caution.l",
    "text": "CAUTION",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.caution.b",
    "text": "Risk of Fire and Burns. Do Not Open, Crush, Heat Above 60 °C or Incinerate. Follow Manufacturer's Instructions.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.d1",
    "text": "Disposal of a battery in fire or a hot oven, or mechanically crushing or cutting of a battery, that can result in an explosion;",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.d2",
    "text": "leaving a battery in an extremely high temperature surrounding environment that can result in an explosion or the leakage of flammable liquid or gas; and",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 0.9766
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "id": "safety.d3",
    "text": "a battery subjected to extremely low air pressure that can result in an explosion or the leakage of flammable liquid or gas.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "id": "maint.h",
    "text": "USER MAINTENANCE INSTRUCTIONS",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "id": "maint.p",
    "text": "During the lifecycle of energy storage products, a certain degree of capacity and energy degradation is expected. As the number of charge and discharge cycles increases and storage time extends, this degradation will gradually intensify, which is a normal phenomenon consistent with the natural aging of battery cells.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
