    "id": "op.caution.l",
    "text": "CAUTION",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "id": "op.caution.i1",
    "text": "USB-C 140W MAX is a USB-PD Power Source 3 (PS3) high-power output port. If the connected user device or accessory does not meet safety requirements, there may be a fire risk. Before using these ports, ensure that the connected device or accessory has fire safety protection.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "id": "op.caution.i2",
    "text": "Only connect the 100D to devices or accessories that comply with clauses 6.3, 6.4, and 6.5 of IEC/EN/UL 62368-1 (or other equivalent standards).",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 0.973
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "id": "op.caution.i3",
    "text": "To obtain maximum output power, use the USB-C to USB-C 5A cable (20V DC/5A, 100W; 28V DC/5A, 140W).",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.eco.h",
    "text": "ENERGY SAVING MODE",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.eco.p1",
    "text": "The Energy Saving Mode is disabled by default. To prevent unnecessary battery drain caused by forgetting to turn off the output, press and hold the DISPLAY button to enable Energy Saving Mode.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.eco.p2",
    "text": "If no device is connected or the connected device's power consumption is below 2W for 2 hours, the product automatically turns off the outputs.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.eco.p3",
    "text": "When the output is on, the icon \"2H\" will appear on the screen.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "fig.eco.press",
    "text": "Press and hold 3s to enable/disable Energy Saving Mode",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.eco.note.l",
    "text": "NOTE",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.eco.note.b",
    "text": "Energy Saving Mode resumes its previous state after powering on. Manual switching is required for mode changes.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.h",
    "text": "LCD SCREEN",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.th1",
    "text": "Function",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.th2",
    "text": "Description",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r1.f",
    "text": "Screen Wake-Up",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r1.d",
    "text": "Lights up when the DISPLAY button is briefly pressed, or automatically during charging or discharging.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r2.f",
    "text": "Screen Always On",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r2.d",
    "text": "While the screen is lit, double-press the DISPLAY button.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r3.f",
    "text": "Screen Switching",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r3.d",
    "text": "After the screen lights up, briefly press the DISPLAY button to switch pages.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r4.f",
    "text": "Turn Off Screen Always-On",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r4.d",
    "text": "Double-press the DISPLAY button again.",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "id": "op.lcd.r5.f",
    "text": "Auto Screen Off",
    "source_ocr_char_coverage": 1.0
  },
  {
